1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,336
Hey, guys...

2
00:00:02,377 --> 00:00:03,378
Wait,
let me tell them.

3
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,379
Sure.

4
00:00:04,421 --> 00:00:05,506
Joey's going to be

5
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:07,466
a celebrity guest
on a game show.

6
00:00:07,508 --> 00:00:09,009
Oh.
Really? Which one?

7
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:14,598
Fish. Seaweed.
A sunken ship.

8
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,891
Things you find
in the ocean.

9
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:17,225
You're going to be
on Pyramid!

10
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:20,980
Oh, it was our favorite
game show ever.

11
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,189
Except for Match Game.

12
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,440
Or Win, Lose or Draw.

13
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:25,734
What did I marry into?

14
00:00:25,776 --> 00:00:27,611
Well, do you guys want
to come down tomorrow

15
00:00:27,653 --> 00:00:28,737
and watch me
tape the show?

16
00:00:28,779 --> 00:00:30,071
Oh, we can't.

17
00:00:30,113 --> 00:00:31,699
We're throwing Phoebe
a bachelorette party.

18
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,408
Yeah, sorry, boys.

19
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,410
This ride's closing.

20
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,579
Well, and Chandler
and I have

21
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,999
this stupid
college alumni thing.

22
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:43,042
I can't believe you get
to meet Donny Osmond.

23
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,170
Seriously?

24
00:00:45,212 --> 00:00:46,380
Yuh-huh!

25
00:00:47,923 --> 00:00:51,677
Ross and I always wanted
to be Donny and Marie.

26
00:00:51,719 --> 00:00:54,221
You guys just keep getting
cooler and cooler.

27
00:00:55,973 --> 00:00:58,433
We used to perform for
our family and friends.

28
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:00,561
Oh, God, that's right.

29
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:02,437
I blocked that out.

30
00:01:02,479 --> 00:01:04,648
♪ I'm a little bit country ♪

31
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:07,150
♪ And I'm a little bit
rock and roll. ♪

32
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:11,655
I'm leaving you.

33
00:01:18,412 --> 00:01:23,000
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

34
00:01:23,042 --> 00:01:25,210
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

35
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:28,839
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

36
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:32,927
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

37
00:01:32,968 --> 00:01:35,094
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

38
00:01:35,136 --> 00:01:37,389
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

39
00:01:37,431 --> 00:01:41,268
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

40
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,812
♪ When the rain starts to pour ♪

41
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:46,314
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

42
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:49,026
♪ Like I've been there before ♪

43
00:01:49,068 --> 00:01:51,779
♪ I'll be there for you ♪

44
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:55,616
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

45
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:08,963
It's so weird to see
all these people again.

46
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:10,839
Oh, my God, look,
there's Jeffrey Klarik.

47
00:02:10,881 --> 00:02:12,091
Who?

48
00:02:12,132 --> 00:02:14,676
He was roommates
with John Rosoff?

49
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:18,472
He went out with
Andrea Tamborino?

50
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:21,308
She dumped him
for Michael Skloff?

51
00:02:22,684 --> 00:02:25,687
Did I go to
this school?

52
00:02:27,898 --> 00:02:29,149
Hey, there's
Missy Goldberg.

53
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,692
You got
to remember her.

54
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:31,819
Sure. Nice.

55
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:34,947
Dude, you're married
to my sister.

56
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:36,573
You're right.
By saying "nice,"

57
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,075
I'm virtually licking her.

58
00:02:38,117 --> 00:02:40,911
Hey, I hear she's
single again.

59
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:43,413
Think I should
ask her out?

60
00:02:43,455 --> 00:02:45,749
Are you asking
permission to
break the pact?

61
00:02:45,791 --> 00:02:47,208
Yes, please.

62
00:03:00,055 --> 00:03:01,222
Hey.

63
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:03,350
Hey, check out the
fliers for the band.

64
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:06,687
I made them on a Macintosh
in the computer room.

65
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:08,522
Awesome.
The name really stands out.

66
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:13,360
Thanks to a little something
called Helvetica Bold 24 point.

67
00:03:13,401 --> 00:03:16,237
Man, we're going to rock
that Asian Student Union!

68
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:19,700
Hey, guys.

69
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,160
Hey, Missy.

70
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,494
Hey, Missy.

71
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:24,454
You know, our band is
playing on Friday.

72
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:26,498
Yeah, yeah, you should come
check us out.

73
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:29,084
We're called "Way/No Way."

74
00:03:29,126 --> 00:03:30,836
No way.

75
00:03:30,878 --> 00:03:32,504
Way!
Way!

76
00:03:32,546 --> 00:03:34,631
Great. I'll
be there.

77
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:35,966
Fresh.
Boss.

78
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,216
Mint.
She's gone.

79
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:38,426
I know it.

80
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:42,890
You know, I'm totally
going to ask her out.

81
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:44,725
Dude, I was going
to ask her out.

82
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,434
I said it first, bro.

83
00:03:46,476 --> 00:03:49,270
Oh, I thought it first, Holmes.

84
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,939
Look, if you think...

85
00:03:50,981 --> 00:03:53,734
Wait, wait.
What are we doing?

86
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:55,903
What we have is
too important

87
00:03:55,944 --> 00:03:58,197
to mess it up
over some girl.

88
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:00,908
I mean, we can get laid
anytime we want.

89
00:04:00,949 --> 00:04:02,034
Totally.

90
00:04:02,076 --> 00:04:04,285
I had sex in high school.

91
00:04:04,327 --> 00:04:05,579
Me, too.

92
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,206
I'm good at it.

93
00:04:08,916 --> 00:04:10,918
All right, I say we make a pact.

94
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:13,837
Neither of us will go out
with Missy Goldberg.

95
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:14,963
You got it.

96
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:18,926
All right, so that's
Missy Goldberg, Phoebe Cates

97
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:21,386
and Molly Ringwald who neither
of us can go out with.

98
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:22,387
Those are the pacts.

99
00:04:22,429 --> 00:04:23,889
Oh, and Sheena Easton.

100
00:04:23,931 --> 00:04:25,891
But we probably couldn't
get her anyway.

101
00:04:25,933 --> 00:04:28,143
Huh! Huh! Maybe not you.

102
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:30,979
Well, I officially

103
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,940
give you permission
to break the pact.

104
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:34,482
Thank you.

105
00:04:37,861 --> 00:04:39,738
All right, here I go.

106
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,615
Now, remember how scary
it used to be

107
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,117
going up to girls in college?

108
00:04:43,158 --> 00:04:44,367
Your hands are shaking.

109
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:47,162
I know, and I can't
stop sweating.

110
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,416
...four, three, applause!

111
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:53,460
( cheering )

112
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:57,798
Yeah!

113
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,258
Welcome.

114
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:00,968
It is Soap Opera Week
here on Pyramid.

115
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:02,427
Let's meet our contestants.

116
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:04,846
First, Gene Lester is
a database specialist.

117
00:05:04,888 --> 00:05:06,848
He's going to be playing
with Days of Our Lives star,

118
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:08,349
Joey Tribianni!

119
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,977
( applause and cheers )

120
00:05:11,186 --> 00:05:12,271
And over here,

121
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,814
we have Henrietta Cherry...

122
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,983
Listen, I know
it can be intimidating

123
00:05:16,024 --> 00:05:18,652
for regular people
to be around celebrities,

124
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:20,403
but relax, I'm just like you,

125
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:22,239
only better-looking
and richer.

126
00:05:22,281 --> 00:05:23,949
...she'll be playing

127
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:26,701
with star
of General Hospital,
Leslie Charleson...

128
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:28,495
( applause )

129
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:29,537
Welcome, everybody.

130
00:05:29,579 --> 00:05:30,747
Good luck to all of you.

131
00:05:30,789 --> 00:05:31,748
Let's play Pyramid.

132
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:32,749
All right.

133
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:34,042
Now, we flipped

134
00:05:34,084 --> 00:05:35,585
a coin before the show.

135
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:37,296
Gene, you won the toss,
so you're going to start.

136
00:05:37,336 --> 00:05:38,588
Which category would you like?

137
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,048
I'll take
"You Crossed the Line."

138
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,675
"You Crossed the Line."

139
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,845
Joey, describe for Gene
these things that have lines.

140
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:47,014
Give me 20 seconds
on the clock, please.

141
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:48,431
Ready. Go.

142
00:05:48,473 --> 00:05:51,518
Uh, okay, it's a store
like a supermarket...

143
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:53,020
( buzzer )

144
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,353
Oh, I see what I did there.

145
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:55,396
Okay, okay.

146
00:05:55,438 --> 00:05:56,690
I'm writing in my...

147
00:05:56,731 --> 00:05:57,691
Diary?

148
00:05:57,732 --> 00:05:58,775
No, more like a notebook--

149
00:05:58,817 --> 00:05:59,776
( buzzer )

150
00:05:59,818 --> 00:06:01,028
Damn it!

151
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:04,531
Um... oh, if I'm
building a house,

152
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:07,159
the plan isn't called
a shmooprint...

153
00:06:07,201 --> 00:06:08,451
( buzzer )

154
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:11,163
I can't do that either?

155
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,748
Oh, in high school,
I once had sex with a girl

156
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,709
right in the middle of the...

157
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:16,584
Cafeteria.

158
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:17,878
Yeah, but that's not

159
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,504
what they're looking for.

160
00:06:19,546 --> 00:06:20,463
( buzzer )
Oh!

161
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:25,927
Thank you so much
for this.

162
00:06:25,969 --> 00:06:27,512
Aw... you like it?

163
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:30,473
Oh, my God, it's
all so elegant.

164
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:32,893
When's the dirty
stuff starting?

165
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,644
What?

166
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:37,147
You know, the strippers
and the guys dancing

167
00:06:37,189 --> 00:06:38,857
and, you know,
pee-pees flying about.

168
00:06:38,899 --> 00:06:39,900
Oh!

169
00:06:42,694 --> 00:06:46,365
Pheebs, I... There isn't
going to be any "flying about."

170
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:47,782
We actually thought

171
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:50,244
we were a little too mature
for stuff like that.

172
00:06:50,285 --> 00:06:52,954
Oh, okay.

173
00:06:52,996 --> 00:06:55,082
I see what you're
doing. That's fine.

174
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:56,457
This is all there is.

175
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,667
Just tea. Okay.

176
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:02,589
Mmm... Raunchy.

177
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:04,174
It's okay.

178
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:05,466
Seriously, Pheebs,

179
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:08,095
it's not going to be
that kind of a party.

180
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:10,264
Really?

181
00:07:10,305 --> 00:07:11,765
So th-this is...

182
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:14,268
this is my big send-off
into married life?

183
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:16,519
Rachel, this is the only
bachelorette party

184
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:17,854
I'm ever going to have.

185
00:07:17,896 --> 00:07:19,898
I've, I've got a big wad
of ones in my purse.

186
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:26,821
Really? I mean really?
It's just tea?

187
00:07:28,489 --> 00:07:31,118
No!

188
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:33,370
Phoebe, of course there's more.

189
00:07:33,412 --> 00:07:34,746
Okay.

190
00:07:34,788 --> 00:07:37,624
I mean, let me just
go talk to Monica

191
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:40,085
and get an ETA on the pee-pees.

192
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:44,672
Gene, I must remind you,

193
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:47,926
you need all six of these
to stay in the game, all right?

194
00:07:47,968 --> 00:07:51,179
Describe for Joey things
you find in your refrigerator.

195
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:53,807
They might as well
just give us the points.

196
00:07:53,848 --> 00:07:55,058
( chuckles )

197
00:07:55,100 --> 00:07:56,393
Give me 20 seconds
on the clock.

198
00:07:56,435 --> 00:07:58,270
Ready. Go.

199
00:07:58,312 --> 00:07:59,813
You put this in your coffee.

200
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:02,523
A spoon! Your hands! Your face!

201
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,400
It's white.

202
00:08:03,442 --> 00:08:06,486
Paper! Snow! A ghost!

203
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:07,904
It's heavier than milk.

204
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:10,615
A rock. A dog. The Earth.

205
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:12,909
Pass. You put this
on a sandwich.

206
00:08:12,951 --> 00:08:15,745
Salami. Anchovies. Jam.

207
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:16,621
It's white.

208
00:08:16,663 --> 00:08:19,498
Paper! Snow! A ghost!

209
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,500
It's made from eggs.

210
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:22,336
Chickens!

211
00:08:22,377 --> 00:08:24,087
Pass!
Oh...

212
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:25,339
You put it on a hamburger.

213
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,340
Ketchup!
Yes.

214
00:08:26,381 --> 00:08:27,382
Relish!
Stop!

215
00:08:27,424 --> 00:08:28,675
( buzzer )
Oh.

216
00:08:28,716 --> 00:08:30,218
Oh, time's up.

217
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:34,473
Joey, you were almost
on a roll there.

218
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:36,266
Gene, you're going
to have a chance

219
00:08:36,308 --> 00:08:38,685
to go to the Winner's Circle
in the second half,

220
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:40,479
but right now, Henrietta,

221
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,730
you are going
to the Winner's Circle

222
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,984
to try your luck for $10,000
right after this.

223
00:08:46,026 --> 00:08:46,985
Don't go away.

224
00:08:47,027 --> 00:08:49,446
And we're out.

225
00:08:49,488 --> 00:08:51,114
Oh, so we didn't win.

226
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:53,783
But it's fun to play
the game, right?

227
00:08:53,825 --> 00:08:55,869
Hey, I got a kid
starting college.

228
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,871
I have to get surgery
on my knee.

229
00:08:57,912 --> 00:08:59,580
You just lost me ten grand.

230
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:02,625
Oh, wow.

231
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,294
I'm so sorry.

232
00:09:04,336 --> 00:09:06,629
Okay, I promise,
we'll do better next time.

233
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,756
Well, I will, because
I won't be playing with you.

234
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:12,886
You know, some of those
were pretty hard.

235
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:16,390
Like, why would there be
a ghost in my fridge?

236
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:20,060
Yeah.

237
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:22,562
So, Saturday night?

238
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:23,563
I'd love to.

239
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:25,065
Great.

240
00:09:27,901 --> 00:09:30,529
So how come it took you
so long to ask me out?

241
00:09:30,569 --> 00:09:33,532
Oh, well, uh, this is
going to sound kind
of silly, but...

242
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:36,201
Do you remember
my roommate Chandler Bing?

243
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:38,786
Sure. He was in your "band."

244
00:09:41,164 --> 00:09:45,377
It's been 16 years,
but the air quotes still hurt.

245
00:09:45,419 --> 00:09:46,378
Sorry.

246
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,962
That's okay.

247
00:09:48,004 --> 00:09:51,091
Anyway, well, he and I both
really liked you a lot, um,

248
00:09:51,132 --> 00:09:53,593
but we didn't want anything
to jeopardize your friendship,

249
00:09:53,634 --> 00:09:57,431
so we kind of made a pact
that neither of us
could ask you out.

250
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:59,015
Really?

251
00:09:59,057 --> 00:10:00,559
Yeah. Why?

252
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:05,397
Well, Chandler and I
used to make out... a lot.

253
00:10:07,982 --> 00:10:09,276
You did?

254
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:12,404
Yeah. We'd go to the
science lab after hours.

255
00:10:12,446 --> 00:10:14,655
And on my turf?!

256
00:10:18,659 --> 00:10:19,994
Hey, where is this guy?

257
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,455
It's been over an hour.

258
00:10:21,496 --> 00:10:22,997
Well, he's coming from Jersey.

259
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:24,832
He said he would get here
as fast as he could.

260
00:10:24,874 --> 00:10:25,959
( pounding on door )

261
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,960
Who is it?

262
00:10:27,001 --> 00:10:28,002
It's the police.

263
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:29,421
The police!

264
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:30,671
